		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Physics programmer needed]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=5449#p5449"><![CDATA[
This well known and respected studio in Montreal is looking for a physics programmer to join their team. Updated!<br><br>•To help develop an ambitious game.<br>•Participate in the design and testing of software in a specific timeframe. <br>•Development of tools and utilities to support the work on the project.<br>Primary Duties:<br>•Develop high quality software using C++ and OOD.<br>•Ability to technically design, implement and review physics systems for use in the development of the game in a specific timeframe.<br>•Ability to optimize and debug code, from low-level libraries through to in game code.<br>•Ability to consider cross platform issues and develop for cross platform API’s.<br>•Generate the highest quality work, leading to the highest quality games.<br>•Ability to schedule own work, and honestly and openly appraise personal and project progress.<br>•Desire to push gameplay technology forward wherever possible.<br>•Positive contribution to team goals, and project focus.<br>At present the studio is still quite small, but they have growth plans that would create a 250-300 person studio in the next two/three years. The studio has a history of developing solid titles and this role will be working on the second installment of a popular and successful title.<br><br>If you would like more information on the role, or if you've never considered Montreal as a place to live and work I'd be happy to discuss with you some of the benefits and why its becoming such a hot-bed of game development. <br>The role offers a significant salary, benefits+++ and full relocation package. Those applying from outside of Canada will also receive full visa sponsorship as required.<br><br>All enquiries should be sent to Ales Chalmners ales {no@spam} amadeusinteractive {dot} com Please add Physx/Montreal in the subject heading.<br><br>Thanks.<br>Ales<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=414">AlesX</a> — Mon Sep 17, 2007